WEBVTT

00:14.990 --> 00:17.820
An arena on the surface,
and a dungeon under it.

00:17.820 --> 00:20.420
I want them to take shape
before the Founder's Festival...

00:20.420 --> 00:23.800
That's a pretty tall order, Great Rimuru.

00:23.800 --> 00:26.920
It's best to assume it'll take
several years for completion.

00:27.400 --> 00:29.550
Yeah, I guess you're right...

00:29.550 --> 00:33.430
Normally thinking, it can't be done
in just a month or two...

00:33.430 --> 00:35.390
Or so I said before...

00:35.900 --> 00:38.140
Yeah, you said that...

00:39.690 --> 00:41.440
It's mostly done already.

00:41.440 --> 00:43.020
Yes, it is.

00:44.860 --> 00:49.280
Let us help build this arena thingy.

00:49.670 --> 00:54.780
Lord Carrion will also participate
in the festival you will be holding.

00:54.780 --> 00:57.660
Please let us help out with that.

00:58.080 --> 01:00.960
You got us a place to live in
and food to fill our stomachs.

01:00.960 --> 01:03.580
If you need help,
just tell us right away.

01:12.260 --> 01:13.590
Thanks to everyone's help...

01:14.550 --> 01:17.990
...we actually managed to get it
into shape in just a month or so.

01:18.520 --> 01:22.650
At this pace, we might get it done
for the Founder's Festival.

01:22.650 --> 01:25.020
Oh, really?

01:25.020 --> 01:26.610
Just leave the rest to us.

01:30.190 --> 01:32.990
I thought I had thrown away
my old common sense...

01:33.490 --> 01:40.330
But seeing things like this really reminds me
that I'm in a whole other world.

01:44.050 --> 01:47.050
THAT TIME I GOT REINCARNATED AS A SLIME

03:11.550 --> 03:12.510
EPISODE 62: THE LABYRINTH AND THE STORM DRAGON

03:12.510 --> 03:14.880
EPISODE 62: THE LABYRINTH AND THE STORM DRAGON
All right, that's a warp for today!

03:15.270 --> 03:17.550
I'll be counting on you guys tomorrow!

03:17.970 --> 03:19.810
Yeah, good work.

03:34.990 --> 03:37.950
I gotta hand it to you, Ramiris.

03:37.950 --> 03:40.490
Your skill Mazecraft is really something.

03:41.490 --> 03:46.080
An ability to transport a massive
space into your labyrinth as is.

03:46.080 --> 03:50.630
The refugee district went straight
into a floor inside the labyrinth.

03:50.630 --> 03:53.130
Thanks to you, everyone's really happy.

03:53.530 --> 03:57.090
There's no rain and the temperature
is just right. They say they love it here.

03:57.090 --> 03:58.590
Hee-hee!

03:58.590 --> 04:01.600
I can add as many floors as you want!

04:01.600 --> 04:04.060
It takes you one hour
to build a floor, right?

04:04.060 --> 04:05.140
Yup!

04:06.430 --> 04:09.150
Let's go with your limit
of one hundred floors, then.

04:09.150 --> 04:11.400
Huh? Why do you need that much?

04:11.400 --> 04:13.730
Since we're doing this,
I want to give it my all!

04:13.730 --> 04:15.570
I want to add various stuff,

04:15.570 --> 04:18.760
and I also want to make it so the monsters
get stronger as you go down.

04:18.760 --> 04:19.780
Fine.

04:19.780 --> 04:22.620
But how do you intend
to add more monsters?

04:22.620 --> 04:24.660
Are you going to capture
'em from somewhere?

04:25.610 --> 04:28.120
Actually, just between you and me...

04:28.120 --> 04:30.290
This and that and this and that...

04:30.290 --> 04:31.750
Oh, I see!

04:31.750 --> 04:33.000
Then how about...

04:35.000 --> 04:37.810
Oh, then how about...

04:39.150 --> 04:41.210
Nice, nice! I like it!

04:41.210 --> 04:43.510
I'll do it! Just you watch!

04:43.880 --> 04:46.350
You can take your time
and rest once in a while, okay?

04:46.350 --> 04:50.900
Heh! How can I take my sweet time
resting after hearing that?

04:51.810 --> 04:53.860
All right, next is...

04:53.860 --> 04:54.900
O-Ouch!

04:57.860 --> 04:59.900
I'm here, Kurobe!

05:00.740 --> 05:02.740
Oh, Great Rimuru!

05:03.170 --> 05:04.740
I've been waiting for you.

05:06.830 --> 05:09.960
All the stuff I store here
has pretty strong quirks,

05:09.960 --> 05:11.920
so not anyone can use them easily.

05:12.330 --> 05:14.210
Are you all right with that?

05:14.210 --> 05:15.380
Of course.

05:15.380 --> 05:18.050
But still, you sure have a lot of them.

05:18.380 --> 05:20.050
Hm? This is...

05:20.570 --> 05:21.510
Analyzing.

05:21.510 --> 05:22.840
Curse Mail.

05:22.840 --> 05:26.810
It absorbs its wearer's magical energy
to erect a magic barrier.

05:26.810 --> 05:28.710
It endlessly absorbs its wearer's energy,

05:28.710 --> 05:31.060
with a high probability of killing its wearer.

05:31.060 --> 05:32.650
Eww.

05:32.650 --> 05:34.060
Then how about this?

05:34.060 --> 05:35.060
Analyze.

05:35.060 --> 05:36.520
Curse Sword.

05:36.520 --> 05:40.030
It absorbs the surrounding magicule
and converts it into explosive force.

05:40.030 --> 05:44.570
It boasts tremendous power,
but it could easily harm its wielder.

05:44.570 --> 05:47.580
Yeah, they all each have
their own strong quirks,

05:47.580 --> 05:50.130
but they're all good stuff.

05:51.080 --> 05:53.790
Receiving praise from you
feels a bit ticklish.

05:53.790 --> 05:54.830
If I remember right...

05:55.250 --> 05:57.250
When I evolved into a Demon Lord,

05:57.250 --> 06:01.170
you received the Unique skill Mastercraft
as your Gift, right?

06:01.880 --> 06:05.430
The skill that turns the quality of
the stuff you make into Rare or above.

06:05.430 --> 06:06.350
Yes!

06:06.820 --> 06:08.430
But what a waste,
don't you think?

06:08.430 --> 06:12.390
Keeping all this high-quality stuff in here
just because it's still in the test stage.

06:12.390 --> 06:16.860
Don't you think they might
want to look for a fitting owner?

06:16.860 --> 06:18.440
Do you think so?

06:18.440 --> 06:20.910
Then please,
take as many as you want.

06:22.240 --> 06:23.570
All right.

06:23.570 --> 06:27.740
Now I've got the stuff to put inside
the dungeon's treasure chests.

06:27.740 --> 06:32.290
I'm sure a lot of Adventurers will gather
in that underground labyrinth.

06:32.790 --> 06:36.040
To crawl into deeper floors,
defeat stronger monsters,

06:36.380 --> 06:39.050
and obtain stronger equipment.

06:39.050 --> 06:42.550
Once that gets going, we will need inns
and equipment stores for the Adventurers,

06:42.550 --> 06:46.800
and appraisals to appraise their findings.

06:47.390 --> 06:51.560
The words about the underground labyrinth
will spread among Adventurers

06:51.560 --> 06:54.560
and in turn, make Tempest itself famous.

06:55.060 --> 06:57.360
That sounds great.

06:58.650 --> 07:01.070
Let me give you this before I forget.

07:01.070 --> 07:04.900
The sword you requested.
It's complete.

07:05.780 --> 07:07.530
It won't break or bend.

07:07.530 --> 07:12.160
I forged it with a focus on durability,
so it can adjust to your magical energy.

07:12.160 --> 07:14.910
It's my best work yet.

07:16.210 --> 07:17.670
So this is it...

07:20.290 --> 07:21.300
Nice!

07:22.300 --> 07:24.300
Not too long, but not too short.

07:24.300 --> 07:27.050
Excellent! You did excellent work, Kurobe!

07:27.050 --> 07:31.220
But that sword is not "complete" yet.

07:31.220 --> 07:36.060
As you requested, I made it
so there's a hole at the base.

07:36.480 --> 07:38.560
But there isn't any hole in this.

07:38.910 --> 07:41.110
This one is special.

07:41.110 --> 07:45.320
It'll grow and evolve by acclimating
to your magical energy

07:45.320 --> 07:48.070
and eventually become
a Legend-class weapon.

07:48.070 --> 07:50.830
Once that happens,
the hole will show itself.

07:50.830 --> 07:52.120
I see!

07:52.120 --> 07:54.790
I will look forward to
when it is complete, then!

07:59.000 --> 08:00.580
Hello, Ramiris!

08:00.950 --> 08:02.340
Have you been well?

08:02.340 --> 08:04.340
Master, long time no see!

08:04.340 --> 08:05.840
Yes, I am fine and well!

08:06.240 --> 08:07.930
I'll be in your care today!

08:07.930 --> 08:09.770
I'll show you the way.

08:12.950 --> 08:15.680
Since Master is here today,
does that mean...

08:15.680 --> 08:17.230
Yeah, that.

08:18.690 --> 08:20.020
Hey, Veldora.

08:20.330 --> 08:22.360
Can you do me a favor?

08:22.360 --> 08:25.400
What? I'm a bit busy right now.

08:25.400 --> 08:27.150
Oh, too bad, then.

08:27.150 --> 08:29.200
I was thinking about
providing a den for you—

08:29.200 --> 08:31.490
What?! My own den?!

08:31.490 --> 08:32.530
Smirk.

08:32.530 --> 08:34.410
I'm all ears.

08:35.200 --> 08:38.580
So Ramiris is actually moving to our town.

08:39.040 --> 08:42.590
So we're gonna build her labyrinth
right underneath the arena.

08:42.590 --> 08:44.340
Oh, Ramiris?

08:44.680 --> 08:49.720
While we're at it, I want to make it great
enough to be our nation's big attraction.

08:49.720 --> 08:52.340
A run-of-the-mill labyrinth
is boring, don't you think?

08:53.430 --> 08:54.600
So?

08:54.600 --> 08:56.810
I think we need one...

08:56.810 --> 08:58.930
...an overlord who reigns
over the dungeon!

08:58.930 --> 09:00.940
An overlord, you say?!

09:01.320 --> 09:03.980
On the hundredth floor,
there's a door that leads

09:03.980 --> 09:06.690
to the spirit labyrinth,
Ramiris's main residence.

09:06.690 --> 09:10.950
So we'll need the strongest guardian
to guard that gate.

09:10.950 --> 09:13.700
Don't you agree,
my good friend Veldora?!

09:13.700 --> 09:16.950
I see! So you want me
to fill in that role, right?!

09:16.950 --> 09:18.080
Yeah!

09:18.080 --> 09:21.790
And if you do it,
you'll get one more bonus.

09:21.790 --> 09:22.670
What?

09:22.670 --> 09:25.380
You have been wanting
to release your Aura, haven't you?

09:25.380 --> 09:27.690
I remember you saying
you're reaching your limit.

09:28.260 --> 09:29.260
You don't mean...!

09:29.260 --> 09:30.340
That's right!

09:30.340 --> 09:33.390
You don't have to hold in
your Aura inside the labyrinth!

09:33.390 --> 09:36.260
You can return to your original
dragon form with no problem!

09:41.600 --> 09:45.150
Well done coming this far, tiny insects!

09:45.150 --> 09:48.670
None of you will escape from me,
the Storm Dragon!

09:54.910 --> 09:57.830
You've done well
to reach out to me, Rimuru!

09:57.830 --> 10:01.460
That is truly a role only I can fulfill!

10:04.670 --> 10:05.920
That's the story.

10:06.350 --> 10:07.380
Easy, right?

10:07.380 --> 10:08.280
Yes, easy.

10:08.920 --> 10:12.800
Now I'm sure he'll release his Aura
well enough in the labyrinth.

10:12.800 --> 10:14.930
With Master's super dense magicule,

10:14.930 --> 10:18.430
monsters will spawn inside
the dungeon in no time!

10:18.430 --> 10:22.940
Yeah! And the closer it is to Veldora,
the stronger the monsters will be.

10:22.940 --> 10:27.150
To take advantage of Master like that...
What a sly guy you are.

10:27.150 --> 10:29.440
Oh, I'm nothing compared to you.

10:29.440 --> 10:31.860
So Ramiris, how's the dungeon doing?!

10:31.860 --> 10:36.120
Hm? Oh, I'm now down to the 15th floor.

10:36.120 --> 10:40.620
At this pace, we should be able to
get to the 100th floor in several days.

10:40.620 --> 10:42.850
The floors will generate
themselves automatically,

10:42.850 --> 10:45.620
so how about we set up
the floors that are done?

10:45.620 --> 10:46.880
All right!

10:46.880 --> 10:49.420
Let's set up Veldora's room first, then.

10:51.880 --> 10:54.630
So this is... my room?

10:56.220 --> 11:00.760
This place kinda reminds me
of the place I was sealed at.

11:00.760 --> 11:02.060
Not to worry, Master!

11:02.430 --> 11:06.150
I can easily add stairs and other things
just by thinking about it!

11:06.150 --> 11:07.440
Oh, for real?!

11:07.440 --> 11:11.440
Then let's use Thought Communication
to decide what kind of room it'll be.

11:13.850 --> 11:15.950
How about this for the interior?

11:18.950 --> 11:22.120
Oooh, yes! This is it, Rimuru!

11:22.120 --> 11:23.450
Well done!

11:23.850 --> 11:27.920
Sounds like he's all up for it.
Think you can make it for us?

11:27.920 --> 11:31.090
Leave it to me.
This much isn't a problem!

11:41.970 --> 11:43.930
You're amazing! This is perfect!

11:43.930 --> 11:46.810
Hee-hee! Yes, I am amazing!

11:46.810 --> 11:50.520
Yes! I am eminently satisfied!

11:51.820 --> 11:53.280
What's this door for?

11:54.860 --> 11:58.490
If you want to read manga,
you'll also need a human-sized room, right?

11:58.490 --> 12:01.660
So I prepared a carpet woven
by Goblina and the others,

12:01.660 --> 12:05.330
a bed that the craftsmen made,
a sofa you can lie on,

12:05.330 --> 12:07.330
and a collection of manga!

12:08.750 --> 12:10.670
Wonderful!

12:10.670 --> 12:13.750
It's perfect!

12:13.750 --> 12:15.340
How nice!

12:15.340 --> 12:18.590
Rimuru, I want some
furniture like this, too!

12:18.590 --> 12:20.590
You worked pretty hard so far, after all.

12:20.590 --> 12:22.640
I'll get them for you
the next time I'm here.

12:22.640 --> 12:24.060
Yay!

12:28.850 --> 12:31.150
I-It's done!

12:31.150 --> 12:34.400
A 100-floor dungeon is complete!

12:34.400 --> 12:37.240
I can't believe we actually
finished it in just a week.

12:37.240 --> 12:39.110
You're really amazing, Ramiris!

12:39.460 --> 12:40.990
Hee-hee!

12:40.990 --> 12:45.370
I made it so the interiors can be
altered freely in the form of blocks.

12:45.370 --> 12:48.160
We can alter the inside on the spot.

12:48.160 --> 12:51.380
A mechanic like this could
easily make any Adventurers cry.

12:51.380 --> 12:55.800
But to put it in another way,
it also means people won't get bored of it.

12:56.880 --> 13:02.050
With this, we can keep the labyrinth
fresh while maintaining its difficulty.

13:02.450 --> 13:07.270
I even made "save points"
every 10 floors as a fail-safe.

13:07.270 --> 13:08.730
Yeah, thanks for that.

13:08.730 --> 13:11.810
If I remember correctly,
you can also do Spatial Motion, right?

13:11.810 --> 13:13.230
Yes, I can!

13:13.230 --> 13:16.810
It won't be affected by outside magicules,
so I can even move humans!

13:16.810 --> 13:19.490
That means as long as they reach
one of these save points,

13:19.490 --> 13:22.320
they can start again
from there next time.

13:23.820 --> 13:27.450
But won't there be people
trying to cheat this system?

13:27.450 --> 13:30.080
Like having friends who are ahead
to bring them along.

13:30.080 --> 13:31.920
Well, I'm sure there will be.

13:31.920 --> 13:32.960
That's why...

13:33.340 --> 13:37.920
I'll station particularly powerful
monsters at the save points.

13:37.920 --> 13:42.300
So you won't be able to use the save point
unless you can defeat it.

13:42.300 --> 13:43.720
I see.

13:43.720 --> 13:49.520
If it's a friend of someone who is capable,
then I doubt they'll do anything funny.

13:49.520 --> 13:52.940
But what if they ended up getting killed?

13:52.940 --> 13:54.940
Yes! That's the point!

13:55.270 --> 13:58.110
That's one of the selling
points of this dungeon!

13:58.110 --> 14:02.610
One of the abilities of
Ramiris's Mazecraft, resurrection!

14:02.610 --> 14:04.200
Resurrection?

14:04.630 --> 14:09.700
Those who form a servitude pact with Ramiris
will become immortal inside Ramiris's labyrinth.

14:10.090 --> 14:13.830
Even if they get killed,
they can get resurrected at the save point!

14:13.830 --> 14:16.210
Ramiris, did you make
the thing I asked for?

14:17.340 --> 14:19.670
Yeah, I did.

14:19.670 --> 14:21.590
Bracelet of Resurrection!

14:21.590 --> 14:22.970
Great.

14:23.510 --> 14:27.100
The problem is how to check
if it really works or not.

14:27.440 --> 14:29.180
Oh, that's okay.

14:29.180 --> 14:32.350
I tried it on Beretta last night.

14:32.350 --> 14:33.440
Hm?

14:34.730 --> 14:35.850
Huh?!

14:37.980 --> 14:39.200
I'm sorry!

14:55.170 --> 14:57.250
Are you okay, Beretta?

14:57.250 --> 14:58.670
Yes...

14:58.670 --> 15:00.670
I am... me.

15:01.010 --> 15:02.710
Yay! It worked!

15:02.710 --> 15:05.430
It was the first test run,
but it was a success!

15:05.430 --> 15:07.730
Huh? The first?

15:08.300 --> 15:09.810
Wait...

15:09.810 --> 15:11.850
What are you doing to her?!

15:12.520 --> 15:17.100
I am a demon, so even in the worst case,
I will not truly perish.

15:17.100 --> 15:19.610
Thanks to you, we know it works.

15:19.610 --> 15:21.690
Good grief.

15:21.690 --> 15:24.240
But I really appreciate it, Beretta.

15:24.240 --> 15:26.030
Good thing it worked!

15:26.030 --> 15:29.990
This is actually my first time
making a consumable item.

15:29.990 --> 15:31.990
You can only use that bracelet once?

15:32.330 --> 15:37.500
You'd need consent to receive an immortal
attribute within Ramiris's Mazecraft world.

15:37.500 --> 15:41.090
But it is predicted that many people
will come to this dungeon.

15:41.090 --> 15:44.510
It'll be tough for Ramiris to form a contract
with every single one of them.

15:44.930 --> 15:48.680
So, to work around that,
this one-time-use consumable item is needed.

15:48.680 --> 15:53.020
This bracelet will only resurrect you
within the labyrinth.

15:53.020 --> 15:55.020
You really thought of everything.

15:55.020 --> 15:58.770
We will think of the price for that later.

15:58.770 --> 16:01.520
Anyway, most of the dungeon is done now.

16:01.520 --> 16:03.440
You did really great, Ramiris.

16:03.440 --> 16:06.780
Now we can finally move
to the next phase of the project!

16:07.240 --> 16:09.620
Hee-hee! Of course!

16:09.620 --> 16:12.280
I'm a woman who can do
things when I wanna to!

16:13.410 --> 16:15.290
Kept you waiting, Veldora.

16:18.120 --> 16:19.960
Finally!

16:19.960 --> 16:22.750
It is finally time for me
to release my Aura!

16:28.760 --> 16:30.090
Well then...

16:30.090 --> 16:31.260
Here I go!

16:43.110 --> 16:43.900
I...

16:46.400 --> 16:47.740
...have appeared!

16:49.030 --> 16:50.360
I...

16:51.240 --> 16:52.870
...am in relief!

16:59.500 --> 17:02.130
Master's really amazing, huh?

17:02.130 --> 17:05.630
I didn't think he'd wreck
my labyrinth like this.

17:05.630 --> 17:08.590
He must've been holding in a lot.

17:10.550 --> 17:12.090
Oh, here it is.

17:12.090 --> 17:13.890
Here it comes!

17:13.890 --> 17:19.100
Master's powerful magicule is
spreading across the labyrinth!

17:19.480 --> 17:21.730
The plan's a success, Rimuru!

17:23.110 --> 17:24.440
Rimuru?

17:24.440 --> 17:26.860
Huh? Oh, umm...

17:27.340 --> 17:28.820
Oho?

17:28.820 --> 17:32.110
You just came up with yet
another scheme, don't you?

17:32.110 --> 17:33.490
Nah.

17:33.490 --> 17:35.700
If he's got such a highly dense magicule,

17:35.700 --> 17:39.350
if we placed the ores we mined here...

17:40.290 --> 17:44.000
They might turn into magistone right away!

17:44.000 --> 17:45.250
Yeah!

17:45.250 --> 17:49.260
We have a plan to import
a large amount of ores.

17:49.650 --> 17:52.790
You really thought of everything, huh?

17:56.010 --> 17:57.680
It's coming out!
It's coming out!

17:57.680 --> 18:00.770
The Aura I've been holding in
is coming out!

18:00.770 --> 18:04.310
From now on, you don't have to hold it in
and can release as much as you want!

18:04.310 --> 18:07.270
But don't do it outside, okay?

18:10.440 --> 18:12.030
Yeah, I know.

18:12.030 --> 18:15.620
Well then, now that we've taken care of
Veldora's problem...

18:15.620 --> 18:17.470
We should take care of this as well.

18:18.540 --> 18:19.910
Beretta.

18:19.910 --> 18:23.620
You declared to Guy
that you'd serve Ramiris, right?

18:24.090 --> 18:26.880
Do you still feel the same way now?

18:30.340 --> 18:32.840
I apologize for being rude,

18:33.630 --> 18:39.390
but as I have stated before,
I wish to serve both you and Lady Ramiris.

18:39.390 --> 18:43.390
But that will go against
your promise to Guy, right?

18:43.830 --> 18:44.710
Yes.

18:45.270 --> 18:47.770
If the time comes, I alone will...

18:47.770 --> 18:50.860
No, no! You don't have to think
too hard about it!

18:51.400 --> 18:54.400
In the end, Ramiris also
moved to this town,

18:54.400 --> 18:57.660
and she's saying she'll work
on managing the dungeon.

18:57.660 --> 19:00.040
And you'll be helping her
with that, right?

19:00.040 --> 19:01.410
Of course.

19:01.410 --> 19:03.830
Then, there's no problem.

19:03.830 --> 19:07.040
In the end, it'll be just as if
you also serve me.

19:07.370 --> 19:09.250
I've been thinking about this for a while.

19:09.250 --> 19:13.800
If you wish for it, I can switch
your allegiances to Ramiris.

19:14.270 --> 19:15.970
Are you okay with that?

19:19.100 --> 19:23.180
If so, I wish to serve Lady Ramiris.

19:23.770 --> 19:24.980
All right.

19:25.520 --> 19:28.940
Well then, Beretta, you may serve
as Ramiris's servant from now on!

19:29.560 --> 19:32.320
I am Lady Ramiris's servant...

19:32.320 --> 19:36.280
but I still remember
the debt I owe to you.

19:36.280 --> 19:40.330
If you need anything from me,
please just say a word.

19:40.710 --> 19:43.110
Yeah. I'll be counting on you then.

19:51.340 --> 19:53.050
Unlocking the Master Lock.

19:54.300 --> 19:57.680
I transfer my ownership to Ramiris!

20:06.940 --> 20:09.560
I have received it.

20:14.320 --> 20:17.930
Please continue to protect
Ramiris for me, Beretta.

20:18.360 --> 20:21.320
I will, even at the cost of my life.

20:21.320 --> 20:25.410
Beretta is now officially my servant...

20:25.410 --> 20:29.080
Now nobody can call me a loner anymore!

20:29.520 --> 20:33.210
Oh my, Lady Ramiris.
You have me as well.

20:33.210 --> 20:34.590
Oh, right!

20:34.590 --> 20:38.800
I also have Treyni. We're turning
into a really big family now!

20:39.770 --> 20:42.510
All right, now that
all the problems are settled,

20:42.510 --> 20:44.180
let's get working
on the dungeon!

20:44.180 --> 20:45.890
Yeah!

20:47.770 --> 20:49.060
Hmm...

20:49.060 --> 20:52.440
With 100 floors, coming up with
a maze sure is daunting.

20:52.840 --> 20:55.320
How about we start with the traps?

20:55.320 --> 20:56.190
I agree!

20:57.690 --> 21:00.200
Poison arrows that fly out of nowhere!

21:00.200 --> 21:03.700
Poison swamps that hurt you when you got
into one and give you status alignment!

21:03.700 --> 21:07.450
How about spinning floors that
mess with your sense of direction?

21:07.450 --> 21:09.090
How 'bout sharp iron wires?!

21:09.090 --> 21:12.210
If you walk through without paying attention,
you will lose your head!

21:12.210 --> 21:17.210
I believe simple traps such as pitfall
can still be very effective.

21:19.470 --> 21:21.260
Yup! I can make all of these.

21:21.260 --> 21:22.680
Really?!

21:22.680 --> 21:24.680
You're really amazing, Ramiris!

21:24.680 --> 21:28.680
I can get pretty much anything
within my labyrinth.

21:28.680 --> 21:29.680
But...

21:29.680 --> 21:32.650
What's this closed room thingy?

21:32.650 --> 21:34.190
How can it be a trap?

21:34.190 --> 21:35.900
Oh, trust me, it will.

21:35.900 --> 21:38.440
There's this material
called oxygen in the air,

21:38.440 --> 21:43.820
and most creatures inhale that
oxygen into their body to live.

21:43.820 --> 21:48.700
If there's extremely little oxygen in the air,
taking a single breath could asphyxiate you,

21:48.700 --> 21:50.870
and maybe even kill you instantly.

21:51.500 --> 21:53.250
Stuff like that.

21:53.250 --> 21:57.460
I've been thinking about this for a while,
but you're scary sometimes, you know that?

21:57.830 --> 21:59.090
You think so?

21:59.090 --> 22:00.840
But also you're reliable.

22:00.840 --> 22:03.640
I can't come up with
a trap like this on my own.

22:03.640 --> 22:06.890
It seems this will become
a hell of a labyrinth.

22:07.390 --> 22:09.810
Do you think we made it
a little too difficult?

22:09.810 --> 22:12.440
This much's nothing for me!

22:12.440 --> 22:15.520
So please! Give more and more ideas!

22:15.520 --> 22:16.650
I see!

22:16.650 --> 22:18.020
Then...

22:18.020 --> 22:21.150
Can you add terrain effects on the floors?

22:21.150 --> 22:22.530
Like a hot floor.

22:22.530 --> 22:23.780
An icy floor.

22:23.780 --> 22:25.240
A stormy floor!

22:25.240 --> 22:28.240
Oh, no, I can't do that.

22:28.240 --> 22:29.200
Terrain effect...

22:29.200 --> 22:30.910
No, I can't do that.

22:30.910 --> 22:34.120
I can't maintain enough energy
to create and manage a terrain like that!

22:34.120 --> 22:35.830
I see...

22:35.830 --> 22:37.960
Yeah, you're right.

22:37.960 --> 22:41.590
I had started to think everything
could be easily solved with magic,

22:41.590 --> 22:44.430
but yeah, a volcano
is a bit too much to ask.

22:44.430 --> 22:47.050
Sorry, Ramiris.
I went a bit too far.

22:47.050 --> 22:48.100
Rimuru...

22:48.100 --> 22:52.020
You can just capture a Fire Dragon
or Ice Dragon and put them here!

22:52.020 --> 22:53.020
Huh?

22:56.560 --> 22:59.400
I could even catch 'em for ya!

22:59.940 --> 23:01.780
What are you doing here?

23:02.280 --> 23:03.570
Milim.

24:36.040 --> 24:38.620
Next time,
"The Audience."
